          "settings": {
            "question": "Will the glass hold up in the wind on Twin Peaks or in the Sunset?",
            "answer": "<p>The panels are 12 mm tempered safety glass, each held in two spigots. The spigot attachments were tested, and the report and blocking details are on our <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-engineering-testing\">engineering page</a>. Wind is a design-load question for the deck as a whole, so your engineer or DBI may ask for those documents. If you want a continuous top edge, the square caprail is available.</p>",
