            "question": "Can a freight truck deliver to a steep street in Bernal Heights or Russian Hill?",
            "answer": "<p>Freight carriers deliver with a liftgate to the curb, and a full-size truck will not fit every San Francisco block. When you order, tell us the street and whether it is steep, narrow or one-way, so the carrier can plan the stop. Sometimes the nearest flat cross street is the practical spot. Have a second person ready to carry the panels up the stairs or through the garage.</p>",
